  "status": "Dismissed",
  "description": "Erection of a 1 x Studio new build dwelling, facilitated by the demolition of the existing storage structure and associated subdivision of the site and landscaping alterations from the host dwelling, with associated cycle and refuse storage and some external alterations and demolitions.",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The principle of residential development\r\nis acceptable within the location. However, due to the incongruous design of\r\nthe building by reason of its diminutive form it is viewed as an anomaly within\r\nthe streetscene, incompatible with the existing built form and an ineffective\r\nuse of the land contrary to Policy 19 and 53 of the adopted Waltham Forest\r\nLocal Plan Part 1 (2024). &nbsp;",
    "The proposed development provides\r\na poor standard of accommodation for future occupiers in relation to (i) an internal\r\nstorage area that fails to comply with minimum space standards, (ii) the\r\nbedroom space located in an incompatible area creating a dead frontage resulting\r\nin the loss of natural surveillance (iii) an external amenity space that fails\r\nto comply with minimum space standards. Therefore, the proposal would be\r\ncontrary to Policy 56 (Residential Space Standards) of the Waltham Forest Local\r\nPlan LP1 (2024), Policy D6 of The London Plan (2021), London Plan Guidance –\r\nHousing Design Standards (June 2023) and the Urban Design SPG (2010)",
    "In the absence of a satisfactory\r\nOutline Construction Logistic Plan, a full assessment&nbsp;of how the proposed\r\ndevelopment would be built or serviced without severely affecting the public\r\nhighway could not be made in line with Policies T7 of the London Plan (2021)\r\nand Policy 65 of the Waltham Forest Local Plan LP1 (2024).",
    "The applicant failed to enter\r\ninto a s106 agreement and therefore not in compliance with Policy 94\r\n(Infrastructure and Developer Contributions) of the Waltham Forest Local Plan\r\nLP1 (2024)&nbsp;(figures applicable at the time of the assessment of the\r\napplication):Car Free Development - the\r\ndevelopment is to be classified as car-free and residents will not be eligible\r\nfor parking permits.A condition survey of the\r\nadjoining carriageway/footwayS106 Financial contribution of £650.00\r\ntowards the Epping Forest SAMMA S106 Financial contribution of\r\n£250 is requested toward CLP monitoring.A S106 contribution of £1,000 is\r\nrequested toward improving walking and cycling facilities within the sites\r\nvicinity which will directly benefit future residents of the site.S278 agreement to remove the\r\nexisting vehicle crossover on Salisbury Road in front of the site; renewal of\r\nthe footway and kerb along the frontage of the site and Extension of the\r\nexisting on-street parking bays across the site frontage.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nFinancial contribution of 5% for\r\ns106 monitoring fees."
  ],
